    "loop": [
      {
        "name": "source-typed-operation-authorization",
        "what": "New input is not admitted as text but as a typed envelope. `Principal` is exactly Human | Agent | Runtime and `Operation` is exactly Queue | Steer | Interject | InterruptAndSend (xai-message-delivery-core/src/envelope.rs:4-16). A `DeliveryEnvelope<Source, Grant, Content, Identity>` carries the principal as a private field plus a `PhantomData<Source>` marker, so `from_human` can only mint a `HumanSource` envelope and `from_agent` only an `AgentSource` one (envelope.rs:35-78). Authorization is a separate, explicit step: `OperationSet` is a bitmask whose only two named values are `QUEUE = 1<<0` and `QUEUE_AND_STEER = (1<<0)|(1<<1)` (envelope.rs:86-102), and `authorize_operation(allowed, requested)` is the single gate. The shell wires it as: humans get `OperationSet::QUEUE`, agents get `OperationSet::QUEUE_AND_STEER` (xai-grok-shell/src/session/message_delivery.rs:138, :171).",
        "invariants": [
          "A human principal may only Queue - the shell passes OperationSet::QUEUE for HumanSource, so Steer is not reachable from a human envelope even though Operation::Steer exists.",
          "The principal is stored, not derived at the call site: callers must use into_parts() and cannot re-label an envelope, because `source` is PhantomData and `principal` is private.",
          "OperationSet has exactly two named constants today; Interject and InterruptAndSend are defined in `Operation` but no code path constructs a set containing them."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed - authorize_operation returns Err(UnsupportedOperation) and the shell maps that to HumanDeliveryError::Unsupported / ActiveMessageAdmission::Unsupported, refusing the input rather than downgrading it to a weaker operation.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "OperationSet::QUEUE",
            "value": "1<<0 (Queue only)",
            "evidence": "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/envelope.rs:90"
          },
          {
            "name": "OperationSet::QUEUE_AND_STEER",
            "value": "(1<<0)|(1<<1)",
            "evidence": "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/envelope.rs:91"
          }
        ],
