      {
        "name": "delivery-envelope-identity-triple-check",
        "what": "Admission of an agent-originated message re-derives and compares three independent facts before the command is queued. The shell recomputes the expected prompt id as the literal `format!(\"parent-message-{}\", message.message_id)` and rejects unless all three hold: `content == message.text`, `message_id == message.message_id`, and `prompt_id == parent-message-{message_id}` (xai-grok-shell/src/session/message_delivery.rs:163-169). Identity itself is a two-field pair `DeliveryIdentity<MessageId, PromptId>` whose constructor is the only way to build it (envelope.rs:22-33); for the human path the two ids are additionally required to be equal, and the grant's target session must match the handle's (message_delivery.rs:135-137). The grant type is the other half of the check: `ResidentHumanGrant{target_session_id}` and `OwnedActiveDescendantGrant{target_session_id, delivery}` are distinct structs, so a caller cannot present an agent grant on a human send path.",
        "invariants": [
          "The prompt-id string `parent-message-{message_id}` is load-bearing and duplicated between the producer and the check; changing the producer format without the check rejects every parent message.",
          "A grant is scoped to exactly one target_session_id; there is no wildcard or inherited grant."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed - any mismatch returns Rejected (human path) or ActiveMessageAdmission::Rejected (agent path) before the mpsc send.",
        "constants": [],
        "evidence": [
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/message_delivery.rs:29-31",
