      {
        "name": "turn-bound-safe-point-delivery",
        "what": "A message that must reach a running turn waits for a safe point instead of cutting in. `MessageDeliveryLifecycle` holds a `VecDeque<DeliverySlot>` where each slot is exactly Pending -> Projecting -> Delivered and each slot carries a `TurnBinding<PromptId, Epoch>` (xai-message-delivery-core/src/lifecycle.rs:74-78, :115-117). The three-phase protocol is explicit: `begin_delivery` moves this turn's Pending slots to Projecting and returns their messages, then `finish_delivery` runs a caller-supplied `commit` closure and only promotes Projecting to Delivered if the commit returns Ok (lifecycle.rs:195-254). A failed commit therefore leaves the messages Projecting, i.e. still unsettled, rather than lost. `transition(TerminalTarget::Turn | All, TerminalCause)` settles everything at end of turn, and the cause decides the disposition - `Completion | SoftCancel | Rewind` fall back (re-queue), while `HardTeardown | ActorDrop` complete as errors (lifecycle.rs:90-103, :256-287). The shell additionally caps live steer slots with `MAX_PARENT_STEER_SLOTS = 32` so one batch of parent text stays finite, and a `Drop` impl settles all slots with a terminal error if the owner disappears (xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:45-47, :83-97).",
        "invariants": [
          "Delivery is not delivery until the commit closure succeeds: Projecting is the only state from which a commit can promote.",
          "A `TurnBinding` is (prompt_id, epoch), not just prompt_id - a rewind that reuses a prompt id but bumps the epoch does not match the old slots.",
          "The lifecycle is append-unique by identity: `admit_pending` returns the message back as Err if that identity is already present in any slot.",
          "ActorDrop must settle every slot: leaving a slot Pending would strand a caller awaiting its oneshot."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed - an uncommitted batch stays Projecting (neither delivered nor dropped) and terminal settlement routes it either to fallbacks (re-queue) or to an explicit error completion; nothing is silently discarded.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "MAX_PARENT_STEER_SLOTS",
            "value": "32",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:47"
          }
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/lifecycle.rs:90-108",
          "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/lifecycle.rs:154-173",
          "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/lifecycle.rs:195-254",
          "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core/src/lifecycle.rs:256-287",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:83-97"
        ],
