      {
        "name": "mid-turn-interjection-framing",
        "what": "Input that arrives while a turn runs is buffered, then drained as synthetic user messages rather than injected as a system note. `InterjectionBuffer<Attachment>` is a type alias for `EventQueue<PendingInterjection<Attachment>>` (xai-interjection-core/src/buffer.rs:24), and `drain_formatted` drains all pending entries and frames each one separately - FIFO, one message per entry, explicitly never merged (buffer.rs:26-42). Framing is a fixed three-part envelope built by `frame_user_turn`: a leading note, the message wrapped by `user_query` in `<user_query>...</user_query>`, and a trailing `UNFINISHED_TASKS_REMINDER` that reads `Make sure to complete any unfinished tasks from previous turns.` (format.rs:8-24). Two notes exist for two situations - `INTERJECTION_NOTE = \"The user sent a message while you were working:\"` for a mid-turn steer and `INTERRUPT_NOTE = \"The user interrupted the previous turn:\"` for the next real query after a text-only mid-turn abort (format.rs:4-5, :43-51). Text longer than `LARGE_PROMPT_THRESHOLD = 25_000` bytes is truncated at a UTF-8 character boundary and suffixed `... [truncated]` (format.rs:1-2, :26-39).",
        "invariants": [
          "The trailing unfinished-tasks reminder is part of the contract, not decoration: every interjection and interrupt carries it, and a test pins that it follows the closing `</user_query>` tag.",
          "One message per buffered entry - `drain_formatted` never merges, which is the opposite of the queued-prompt combine rule in xai-prompt-queue.",
          "Truncation must land on a char boundary; the implementation walks char_indices rather than slicing at the byte offset."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft - oversize text is truncated with a visible marker rather than rejected; an empty buffer drains to an empty vec, and sanitization is a caller-supplied function whose absence is spelled as `std::convert::identity`.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "LARGE_PROMPT_THRESHOLD",
            "value": "25_000 (bytes)",
            "evidence": "crates/common/xai-interjection-core/src/format.rs:2"
