      {
        "name": "queued-prompt-combine-with-versioned-edit",
        "what": "Follow-up prompts queued behind a running turn can be merged into one turn under a pure, shared eligibility rule. `combine_prefix_len` walks the queue from the front and returns the mergeable prefix length: the front must be a plain prompt (`can_merge_front` - not synthetic, not an expanded skill, not bash, non-empty text, images allowed) and each follower must additionally carry no images and not be under edit hold (`can_merge_follower`) (xai-prompt-queue/src/combine.rs:29-60). Merged bodies are joined with a blank-line separator `TEXT_SEPARATOR = \"\\n\\n\"` (combine.rs:9, :62-68) and, when two or more originals merged, the per-prompt display texts are stamped into content-block `_meta` under `COMBINED_DISPLAY_TEXTS_META = \"combinedDisplayTexts\"` so the UI can rebuild multi-bubble display from one model turn (types.rs:3-5, combine.rs:70-93). Queue rows are edited in place under optimistic concurrency: `QueueEntryMeta.version` is a monotonic counter bumped on every edit and `owner` is explicitly never overwritten by edits, only `last_editor` is (types.rs:10-26). The whole queue is mirrored to clients as one `QueueChanged` broadcast keyed by `sessionId`, carrying `entries` plus a separately-reported `running_prompt_id`/`running_text` because the running row is deliberately omitted from `entries` (types.rs:53-76).",
        "invariants": [
          "Eligibility for merging lives in one pure module shared by the pager's local drain and the shell's promote path, so the stop conditions cannot drift between them.",
          "The running row is never present in `entries`; a client must read `runningPromptId`/`runningText` or it will show a queue with a hole.",
          "`owner` is immutable under edit - only `last_editor` moves.",
          "A `QueueChanged` without `sessionId` must fail to parse rather than apply under the wrong key."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft - an ineligible front yields prefix length 1 (take the front alone), so combining simply does not happen; an unknown extra field deserializes and is ignored for forward compatibility.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "TEXT_SEPARATOR",
            "value": "\"\\n\\n\"",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-prompt-queue/src/combine.rs:9"
