        "name": "canonical-turn-event-log",
        "what": "Each session writes an append-only `events.jsonl` whose rows are a pinned, tagged event taxonomy rather than free-form logging. `EVENT_SCHEMA_VERSION = \"1.0\"` is stamped on the turn-scoped rows (xai-grok-session-events/src/types.rs:3, :15), and `Event` is a `#[serde(tag = \"type\", rename_all = \"snake_case\")]` enum covering the loop's observable states: TurnStarted (with turn_number, model_id, yolo_mode, conversation_message_count, session_relationship), PhaseChanged, FirstToken, LoopStarted{loop_index}, ToolStarted, ToolCompleted (duration_ms, outcome, source, rewriting_hook), PermissionRequested, PermissionResolved (decision, wait_ms), TurnEnded (outcome, cancellation_category, cancellation_context), Interjected (source, image_count, redirect_kind) and YoloToggled (types.rs:5-62). The `EventTracker` holds the mutable per-turn counters the events are derived from - active tool, tool count this turn, and one-shot `prior_interrupt_category` / `prior_redirect_kind` markers that survive `begin_turn` (tracker.rs:84-183).",
        "invariants": [
          "`schema_version` is a field on the turn-scoped rows, so a reader can branch per row rather than per file.",
          "The prior-interrupt and prior-redirect markers are one-shot `take_*` values that deliberately survive begin_turn; they describe the previous turn, and a test pins that.",
          "Wire labels are pinned by test: tool outcomes, cancellation categories, redirect kinds and interjection tags must round-trip."
