        "name": "single-source-token-estimation",
        "what": "Token accounting is one shared, deliberately crude heuristic rather than per-consumer arithmetic. The crate doc states the intent plainly: it is the single source of truth for the bytes/4 heuristic and the derived-display arithmetic used by `/context`, `/session-info`, the auto-compact gates, the preflight overflow check, and every client renderer (xai-token-estimation/src/lib.rs:1-6). The primitives are `estimate_tokens`/`estimate_chars` over `BYTES_PER_TOKEN = 4` and a separate flat `IMAGE_TOKEN_ESTIMATE = 765` applied per image by `estimate_image_tokens` (lib.rs:9, :13, :17-31). Threshold decisions are also centralized: `exceeds_threshold` and `exceeds_threshold_with_headroom` are the only predicates, and percentage display is split into three variants (`usage_percentage`, `usage_percentage_u8`, `usage_percentage_truncated_u8`) so a renderer picks a rounding behaviour instead of inventing one (lib.rs:38-89).",
        "invariants": [
          "Every consumer that talks about context-window usage must route through this crate; the crate doc explicitly enumerates the five consumers so a new one is a visible addition.",
