      {
        "name": "full-replace-compaction-rather-than-tail-retention",
        "what": "grok's compaction is a FULL REPLACE: it summarises the whole conversation and rebuilds a fresh history rather than keeping a recent tail, so there is no tail-budget or split-point policy on the shipped path. `sample_summary_with_retries` calls the compaction sampler up to `max_attempts` times, accepting a non-empty summary whose cleaned seed passes `is_degenerate_summary`, treating empty or degenerate output as transient, and short-circuiting deterministic failures (xai-grok-compaction/src/code_compaction/compact.rs:53-73, :87-98). Failures are returned structurally as a typed error carrying `message`, `deterministic` and `context_overflow` so the host can choose between suppressing auto-compaction and stepping its own input ladder. The lossy summary is then made recoverable by a pointer, not by retained turns: `CompactionMode` is Summary (no pointer), Transcript (pointer to the raw `updates.jsonl`) or Segments(CompactionDetail), and `transcript_hint` returns None if the mode adds no pointer OR no location is available, so the model is never pointed at nothing (xai-chat-state/src/compaction_mode.rs:12-25, :49-83). `CompactionDetail` is a separate four-level axis (None/Minimal/Balanced/Verbose, default Verbose) that attaches only to Segments.",
        "invariants": [
          "A context-length overflow must be reported with BOTH `context_overflow` and `deterministic` set, because re-sending the same payload is guaranteed to fail again - retrying it is pure waste.",
          "`CompactionMode::default()` must stay `Segments(CompactionDetail::default())`, i.e. Verbose; this is the shipped default and a change silently reduces recoverable detail.",
          "Detail must attach only to `Segments` - the other modes ignore it, so attaching it elsewhere would expose a meaningless setting.",
          "The retry loop must stay content-neutral: the harness builds the prompt and cleans the winning summary, so the loop cannot bias content."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed to the caller - a typed terminal error and no partially applied compaction; individual transient attempts are retried after a delay.",
