        "wiringNote": "Mostly INERT in this tree. The crate is a real engine (36 src files, no cargo features) and the shell does call `sample_full_replace_summary` (xai-grok-shell/src/session/compaction.rs:1138), but `apply_intra_compaction`, `should_compact`, `inter_compaction`, `history::filter`/`history::validate`, `select.rs`, `fit.rs`, `assemble_compacted_history`, `apply_full_replace_compaction`, `wrap_user_query` and `validate_compaction_text` have callers only inside the crate's own tests - the shell uses xai-chat-state's duplicated `compaction_utils` copies instead. `IntraCompactionConfig::default()` sets `enabled: false` (crates/common/xai-grok-compaction/src/intra_compaction/config.rs:227). The tool-pair-safe split selector in particular is UNWIRED: `select_turns_to_compact` walks backward accumulating keep-tokens and `snap_to_safe_boundary` advances past a contiguous run of tool results so a split can never orphan a tool result, returning None rather than 'compact everything' when nothing should move (crates/common/xai-grok-compaction/src/select.rs:60-147) - but its only callers are intra_compaction/compact.rs:505 and fit.rs:148, in the unwired chain."
      },
      {
        "name": "boundary-exact-token-gate-and-image-budget-hysteresis",
        "what": "Two distinct budget mechanisms with deliberately different shapes. (a) The token gate is boundary-exact integer arithmetic: `exceeds_threshold` computes `used*100 >= window*threshold` so it fires exactly AT the threshold, which is one token earlier than a legacy `>` gate, and `exceeds_threshold_with_headroom` is the same scaled comparison minus `headroom*100` (xai-token-estimation/src/lib.rs:78-102). The display helpers deliberately differ from each other - `usage_percentage_u8` ROUNDS while `usage_percentage_truncated_u8` TRUNCATES - because a test pins that `exceeds_threshold(used, window, p)` agrees with `truncated(used, window) >= p` (lib.rs:48-64). (b) Image eviction is a hysteresis loop rather than a threshold: `apply_image_budget` measures the exact serialized conversation body and evicts inline images oldest-first only when the body reaches a high-water trigger, reclaiming down to a strictly lower low-water mark (xai-chat-state/src/image_budget.rs:20-60). Measurement is exact but allocation-free: `conversation_body_bytes` blanks every image URL, serializes through a byte-counting `io::Write` sink, then adds back each URL's exact escaped contribution (image_budget.rs:244-321).",
        "invariants": [
          "`exceeds_threshold` must keep `>=` semantics and the `context_window == 0 -> false` short-circuit, or callers would have to special-case a missing window.",
          "`usage_percentage_truncated_u8` must keep truncating while `usage_percentage_u8` rounds; collapsing them breaks the agreement test between the gate and the displayed number.",
          "All products in the gate must stay saturating so a huge window cannot wrap.",
          "The image reclaim target must stay strictly BELOW the trigger - this is enforced by a compile-time assert, because otherwise every turn at the ceiling re-evicts and re-busts the prompt cache.",
          "Below the trigger the request history must stay byte-identical so the KV prefix remains stable."
        ],
