      {
        "name": "concurrent-tool-dispatch-with-per-path-serialization",
        "what": "A batch of tool calls is prepared sequentially - approval, hooks, argument remapping - then dispatched concurrently, and each result is committed to state as it arrives rather than after the whole batch. `execute_tool_calls` splits an `exit_plan_mode` tail out of a multi-call batch so plan approval acts as a barrier, then runs the two batches in order (xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/tool_calls.rs:384-437). `execute_tool_calls_batch` builds one future per approved call, pushes them into a `futures::stream::FuturesUnordered`, and drains them through an unbounded channel in a completion loop that takes the matching approved slot and runs post-tool-use handling per item (tool_calls.rs:935-960). Write conflicts are serialized by a per-path `tokio::sync::Mutex` map built only from calls whose `is_read_only` is false (tool_calls.rs:653-670, :815-823), and `lock_path_for_args` canonicalizes the existing ancestor so two spellings of the same file share one lock (xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/tool_dispatch.rs:53-86). A separate FIFO lock manager with writer-starvation avoidance exists beneath at `FileOperationLockManager` (xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/editor_infra/file_operation_lock.rs:1-114).",
        "invariants": [
          "Two calls keying the same path must share a lock and therefore run in model-emitted order; returning no key is what means genuinely concurrent.",
          "A read-only call must never enter the write-lock set.",
          "One index maps to exactly one approved slot - the completion loop takes rather than indexes.",
          "A permission rejection on any call must still answer every remaining call in the batch with a cancelled result so the provider's call/result pairing stays intact."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "mixed - the stream-drain barrier before emitting calls is fail-open on timeout (proceed) but a revoked boundary aborts the turn; a permission reject fails the batch closed while still pairing every tool_result.",
