      {
        "name": "backoff-ladder-plus-server-signalled-doom-loop-recovery",
        "what": "There are two independent retry systems and they are deliberately not the same one. Generic exponential backoff is `BackoffConfig { max_retries, base_delay_ms, max_delay_ms }` with `calculate_delay` doubling and clamping to the cap, driven by `execute_with_backoff` which invokes an `on_retry(attempt, max, delay)` callback before sleeping (xai-grok-tools/src/retry.rs:11-95); live call sites use 5 retries / 5 s base / 60 s cap for the model catalog and 5 / 2 s / 30 s for a post-unblock JWT retry. Repeat-tool and doom-loop recovery is NOT client-detected: the server emits a non-standard `response.doom_loop_check` SSE event with a cumulative trigger set, parsed into a signal type with an `Unknown` fallback (xai-grok-sampling-types/src/doom_loop.rs:33, :169-195), governed by a recovery policy and retried under its own backoff (xai-grok-sampler/src/retry.rs:30). Turn-level transient retries are separately bounded (xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/sampler_turn.rs:19-30, :66-72).",
        "invariants": [
          "Tool failures are explicitly not fed to the doom-loop detector - error-count streaks were removed as a signal.",
          "`DoomLoopSignal::parse` must never fail: any grammar mismatch becomes `Unknown` with the raw label preserved, so a server-side evolution cannot break the client.",
          "Only a confident trigger set resamples - an `Unknown` signal degrades rather than triggering recovery.",
          "The doom-loop marker is ignored when it appears inside a text delta; it is matched as a structured event, not by substring."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft - an unparseable or unconfident signal degrades to no recovery; transient turn retries are bounded by both a count and a wall-clock window so retries cannot continue indefinitely.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "DOOM_LOOP_CHECK_EVENT_TYPE",
            "value": "\"response.doom_loop_check\"",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-grok-sampling-types/src/doom_loop.rs:33"
          },
          {
            "name": "MAX_TRANSIENT_TURN_RETRIES",
            "value": "3",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/sampler_turn.rs:19"
