      {
        "name": "lazy-tool-exposure-via-search-index",
        "what": "Not every available tool is exposed to the model at once. A `ToolSearchIndex` trait is defined in the tools crate precisely to stay backend-agnostic, implemented in the shell, and returns a `SearchSnapshot { results, total_hidden_tools, is_ready }`; a `ToolIndex` wraps it as an injected resource (xai-grok-tools/src/types/tool_index.rs:29-74). The model reaches hidden tools through `search_tool` / `use_tool` meta-tools. The readiness flag is part of the contract rather than an internal detail: `is_ready = false` means the index is still warming and results may be incomplete, which consumers must distinguish from a genuine no-match (tool_index.rs:35-37).",
        "invariants": [
          "The trait must carry no MCP-specific concepts - the concrete implementation maps its own initialization state onto `is_ready`.",
          "`is_ready = false` must be surfaced, not collapsed into an empty result, or a cold index reads as 'this tool does not exist'.",
          "A static index must be `Send + Sync` because it is injected as a shared resource."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-open on index warmth (partial results are returned with the flag set) and fail-closed on call time (an unavailable tool cannot be invoked).",
        "constants": [],
        "evidence": [
