    "subagent": [
      {
        "name": "harness-only-subagent-capability-mode",
        "what": "A subagent's tool inventory is narrowed by a four-valued capability mode - ReadOnly | ReadWrite | Execute | All - applied by filtering the tool config on each tool's `ToolKind` (xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/types.rs:289-305). `filter_tool_config` returns immediately for `All`, otherwise retains only tools whose kind is in `allowed_tool_kinds()`, and then calls `prune_orphaned_background_task_tools`, which drops `get_task_output`/`kill_task` when no spawning tool remains so a read-only subagent is not handed lifecycle verbs for tasks it cannot create (types.rs:254-300). The mode is harness-only: it is `Option<SubagentCapabilityMode>` on the runtime overrides and is deliberately absent from the model-facing JSON schema, with tests asserting both that the schema omits `capability_mode` and that a model-supplied `capability_mode` in JSON does not round-trip (types.rs:1790-1864). The mode is set from the host side by the role that spawns the agent - for example the goal summarizer pins `SubagentCapabilityMode::ReadOnly` so the summariser can inspect but never edit or execute (xai-grok-shell/src/session/goal_summarizer.rs:140, :160).",
        "invariants": [
          "capability_mode must never be advertised on the model-facing tool schema, and a model-authored value must be ignored - the tests exist precisely to keep this boundary.",
          "Tools with no `kind` (MCP and custom tools built via `ToolConfig::from_id`) are preserved unconditionally, so an MCP tool is NOT narrowed by capability mode.",
          "Pruning background-task lifecycle tools is a consequence of the filter, not a separate opt-in."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed on inventory (the tool config is narrowed before the subagent starts) but with an explicit fail-open carve-out for kindless MCP/custom tools.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "SubagentCapabilityMode variants",
            "value": "read-only | read-write | execute | all",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/types.rs:1870-1877"
          }
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/types.rs:239-305",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/types.rs:1828-1832",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/types.rs:1842-1864",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/goal_summarizer.rs:140-160"
        ],
        "modules": [
          "xai-grok-tools",
          "crates/common/xai-tool-types",
          "xai-grok-shell"
        ],
        "verified": true
      },
      {
        "name": "parent-wake-safe-point-admission",
        "what": "A resident subagent can receive text from its owning parent while a turn is running, but only through the same turn-bound lifecycle as human input, and only if the sender owns an active descendant. The shell route is `SessionCommand::ParentAgentMessage`, and the message is converted into an `InputItem` carrying queue metadata of kind `parent_agent_message` so it appears in the shared queue with honest provenance (xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:99-120). The grant is `OwnedActiveDescendantGrant`, which pairs a target session id with the `ActiveAgentMessageDelivery` it authorizes, and the handle rejects any mismatch with its own target session before doing anything else (message_delivery.rs:159-161). Live steer slots are bounded by `MAX_PARENT_STEER_SLOTS = 32` so a parent's text becomes model-visible in one finite batch (parent_message.rs:45-47). The operation a parent may request is restricted to Queue or Steer - `delivery_operation` maps only those two `ActiveAgentMessageOperation` variants, and the envelope is additionally checked against `OperationSet::QUEUE_AND_STEER` (message_delivery.rs:98-103, :170-174).",
        "invariants": [
          "The parent must own an active descendant: the grant is a distinct type carrying both target session and delivery, and there is no path that constructs it for a non-descendant.",
          "A parent cannot use Interject or InterruptAndSend - only Queue and Steer are mapped, and the operation set check would reject the others.",
          "The completion channel is a oneshot `PromptTurnResult` that must be settled on every path, including owner drop."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed - Rejected / Unsupported / ChannelClosed are returned to the caller and the message is not queued; the Drop impl settles stranded slots with an explicit error rather than leaving the parent awaiting.",
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "MAX_PARENT_STEER_SLOTS",
            "value": "32",
            "evidence": "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:47"
          }
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:45-47",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/acp_session_impl/parent_message.rs:83-120",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/message_delivery.rs:98-103",
          "crates/codegen/xai-grok-shell/src/session/message_delivery.rs:146-192"
        ],
        "modules": [
          "xai-grok-shell",
          "crates/common/xai-message-delivery-core"
        ],
        "verified": true
      },
      {
        "name": "capability-mode-meet-and-resume-identity-pin",
        "what": "A subagent's effective runtime config is resolved by first-wins precedence per field, and its capability mode is then narrowed by a meet rather than replaced. Precedence is explicit spawn-time override > role default > persona default > None meaning parent inheritance, with role and persona defaults looked up by name (xai-grok-subagent-resolution/src/overrides.rs:39-49). `intersect_capability_modes(requested, ceiling)` is the narrowing operator and its behaviour is a deliberate lattice: (None, mode) or (mode, None) yields mode; any pair containing `All` yields the other; any pair containing `ReadOnly` yields `ReadOnly`; equal ReadWrite or equal Execute yield themselves; and the incomparable pair ReadWrite/Execute collapses to `ReadOnly` (overrides.rs:22-37). Resume is gated on identity rather than on configuration: `validate_resume_identity` rejects a mismatched subagent type or an explicitly requested persona that differs from the source, while a model override is deliberately NOT validated and is silently ignored because the resumed child always inherits and pins the source model (resume.rs:1-6, :33-60).",
        "invariants": [
          "The capability meet must stay most-restrictive-wins: the ReadWrite/Execute pair must not resolve to either input, and `All` must never win against a narrower mode.",
          "Resume inherits the source transcript, tool state and model but re-renders the system prompt and prompt context from the current agent definition - the two halves move differently on purpose.",
          "Model is not an identity gate on resume; a caller-supplied model override is ignored rather than rejected, so it must not be surfaced as an error.",
          "A persona instructions-file read failure is fatal to resolution and returns early with the error populated rather than silently falling back to the parent."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "mixed - identity and persona-file failures are fail-closed (resolution aborts or resume is refused), while a model override on resume is fail-safe by being silently dropped in favour of the pinned source model.",
        "constants": [],
