        "name": "targeted-cancellation-with-closed-admission-window",
        "what": "A single-writer coordinator actor owns the spawn queue, the pending/active/completed maps, blocking waiters, foreground deadlines, cancellation and terminal delivery, with intentionally no shared mutable state; hosts differ only in their child-runner implementation (xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/coordinator.rs:53). Cancellation is TARGETED rather than global - the target is a subagent id, a parent prompt id, a parent session, or a workflow run id - and a parent-session cancel additionally keeps spawn admission CLOSED until the next turn or until teardown completes, so a detached late spawn cannot outrun a stop or a session delete (xai-grok-shell/src/agent/subagent/spawn.rs:284; task/types.rs:541, :590).",
