        "what": "A task call waits only for a bounded foreground budget. Past the deadline the child is auto-backgrounded with a log line noting it keeps running, an INTERIM result is sent carrying a backgrounded flag and success set to false so no consumer records a completed status for a live child, and the deadline is cleared so the check cannot re-fire (xai-grok-tools/src/implementations/grok_build/task/coordinator_state.rs:606, :623, :639). A sibling path covers a dropped result channel: a task-owned child keeps running and leaves the outstanding set, while a workflow-owned child is cancelled.",
