      {
        "name": "mcp-elicitation-single-slot-rendezvous",
        "what": "Server-initiated `elicitation/create` is forwarded to the client as the ACP request `x.ai/mcp/elicit`, with completion notified as `x.ai/mcp/elicit_complete` (xai-grok-mcp/src/wire.rs:28). The inbox is a single-slot rendezvous - a mutex-guarded optional job plus a notify - where push REPLACES any previous job, close cancels the outstanding one, and receive returns nothing once closed (xai-grok-mcp/src/elicitation.rs:63, :108). Message size, URL length, id length and schema bytes are all validated AT INGEST against caps defined in the tools crate, so a consumer never observes an unsupported mode or an oversized schema (xai-grok-mcp/src/elicitation.rs:178-181; xai-grok-tools/src/mcp_elicitation/schema.rs:9-17).",
        "invariants": [
          "Only one elicitation can be outstanding by construction, and a second REPLACES the first while also answering the displaced one with a cancel result - replacing without answering would strand the server.",
          "Size and charset validation happens before enqueue, not at consumption.",
          "On an unsupported mode the bridge must DECLINE rather than error, because the MCP server needs a valid result either way.",
          "The bridge is not advertised on the zero-IPC ACP transport, so a compliant in-process server never sends elicitation there."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft and closed toward the server, never toward the user - an unsupported mode declines, a missing bridge declines, a closed channel cancels, and a dropped oneshot cancels.",
