        "what": "A marketplace catalogue layers over an existing install-registry pipeline. Sources come from configured marketplace entries (a local path, or a git URL with an optional branch) plus vendor-compat settings files; git sources are cloned shallowly into a persistent cache under a hash of the URL, behind an fs2 file lock with a TTL consumed through an RAII lease (xai-grok-plugin-marketplace/src/config.rs:34; src/git.rs:16-20, :240). The official source is auto-registered once on first run behind a flag. Installs route either through a local copy from the synced checkout or through a remote clone pinned to a `git_sha` when the index provides one, and the host exposes the surface over ACP list and action methods (xai-grok-shell/src/extensions/marketplace.rs:20).",
        "invariants": [
          "Plugins are NOT cryptographically signed, and an unpinned remote install tracks a mutable ref - publishing a sha in the plugin index is the documented mitigation, so `require_sha` is a policy control rather than a verification control.",
          "`require_sha` is TIGHTEN-ONLY: config or environment can turn it on and neither can turn it off, so a user-writable layer cannot weaken an admin's pin.",
          "`require_sha` covers every remote-fetch path but NOT plugins vendored inside a marketplace source checkout - the gap is structural, not an oversight to be assumed away.",
          "The official-source comparison must normalize case, a leading www, trailing slashes and .git, and the HTTPS/SSH/scp URL forms before matching."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "mixed - `require_sha` fails an unpinned remote install closed, a hung git network operation is killed at a timeout and reported, and a malformed marketplace source entry warns and is skipped while the rest of the file still parses.",
