      {
        "name": "workflow-rhai-engine-with-journal-replay",
        "what": "Workflows are Rhai scripts executed against a host-function surface of agent, parallel and the complete/pause/emit family, and every host call is content-hashed and appended to an append-only journal keyed by a dense sequence number (xai-workflow/src/engine.rs:492, :511; src/journal.rs:39). A re-run REPLAYS recorded results instead of re-spawning agents, and a hash mismatch raises a divergence error stating that the script is nondeterministic or was edited mid-run. The outcome type admits Completed, Paused with a reason, BudgetExceeded, Cancelled and Failed, with pause reasons distinguishing user, back-off, no-progress, verification and infra (xai-workflow/src/run.rs:5).",
        "invariants": [
          "The journal must be dense and bounded BEFORE restore: loading rejects a restore whose size or entry count would exceed the cap, so a run can never be written into an unresumable state.",
          "Replay must stay deterministic - host-call order and hash ARE the identity, so a mid-run script edit is a fatal divergence rather than a silent re-execution.",
          "Parallel items must be option maps.",
          "Terminal outcomes must never be demoted by a later event."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-closed on journal integrity (an unsafe restore, a sequence gap or a divergence all abort the run) and fail-soft on a live host call, which is recorded as a sentinel so a resume can retry it.",
