      {
        "name": "hybrid-bm25-plus-vector-memory-retrieval",
        "what": "The memory retrieval pipeline fuses lexical and vector search rather than choosing one. FTS5 BM25 runs against a supplemental evergreen query over both the global and workspace scopes so curated memory is not crowded out by session volume, optionally joined by a sqlite-vec KNN pass with an absolute L2-to-similarity normalization; per chunk the merge is `max(text_weight*fts + vector_weight*vec, fts)` so the lexical score is a floor rather than a component (xai-grok-memory/src/search.rs:183, :274-285). On top of the fused score come exponential temporal decay, per-source weights, and an access-frequency boost of `1 + ln_1p(access_count)*0.05`, then an MMR diversity re-rank before truncating to `max_results` (search.rs:323-331; xai-grok-memory/src/mmr.rs:52-62).",
        "invariants": [
          "Ranking and MMR must use the unclamped raw score, never the clamped `SearchResult::score` - `mmr_rerank` takes a separate index-aligned relevance slice and asserts equal lengths.",
          "Evergreen sources must keep decay at 1.0 and are the only sources subject to the scaffold-marker filter.",
          "`&MemoryIndex` must never be held across an `.await` because rusqlite is `!Send` - which is why the pipeline is phased sync/async/sync.",
          "Candidate generation must oversample: `candidate_limit = max_results * 3`, so the re-rank has material to work with."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "mixed. Ranking degrades fail-open (FTS errors become empty via `unwrap_or_default()`, vector errors log and set `is_vector_degraded` while reporting an FTS-only mode, and a failed query embedding yields an embedding-fallback marker). Opening the index is the one hard error. Scoping a credential to an embedding endpoint fails CLOSED: an untrusted or mismatched endpoint drops the scoped credential rather than sending it.",
