      {
        "name": "incremental-content-hash-reindex-over-contentless-fts",
        "what": "The markdown-to-searchable-rows write path is hash-diffed rather than rebuilt. `chunk_markdown` splits on ATX headers with paragraph and line fallbacks, short-circuits small content, overlaps continuation chunks, and prepends ancestor context as `[Context: ## A > ### B]` (xai-grok-memory/src/chunker.rs:141). `MemoryIndex::reindex_file` hashes each chunk with blake3 against existing rows keyed `\"{path}:{chunk_index}\"` and applies insert, update and delete plus FTS and vector maintenance inside ONE transaction (xai-grok-memory/src/index.rs:244-271, :617). Deletion is idempotent and removes a file's chunks from all three tables at once.",
        "invariants": [
          "The chunk id must stay `\"{path}:{index}\"` with deterministic chunk ordering, because hash-diffing relies on positional ids.",
          "`chunks_fts` is CONTENTLESS (`USING fts5(text, content='')`), so a delete must re-supply the original stored text - dropping the chunk text column breaks deletion.",
          "Chunk, FTS and vector mutations must remain in one transaction, or the three tables desynchronize."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft - an unreadable file warns and returns a default result, per-chunk vector deletes and upserts discard their errors, unresolvable FTS rowids are silently dropped, and a failed embedding batch is logged and skipped. Only SQL errors propagate.",
