      {
        "name": "bm25-fts5-session-index-with-lease-fenced-bootstrap",
        "what": "Cross-session search over historical transcripts uses a content-synced FTS5 table: one `session_docs` row per session plus `session_docs_fts(title, content)` kept in sync by insert/delete/update triggers, so callers only ever write the base table (xai-grok-session-search/src/fts.rs:26, :565-577). Ranking is `bm25(session_docs_fts, 10.0, 1.0)` - the title weighted ten times the body. The cwd filter is applied through a JOIN rather than by indexing cwd, every token is quoted as a prefix, an AND query runs first and falls back to OR only when the AND total is zero, and UUID-like or 8-plus-hex-character queries are served through an `instr(lower(session_id), lower(?))` substring path instead of the FTS index (fts.rs:705). Full reindex is cross-process single-flight: one atomic upsert claims bootstrap when the stored stamp is expired OR in the future (clock rollback), stamping `\"{unix_secs}:{uuid}\"`, and every claim-scoped write is fenced on that token so a stale claimant can never assert completion or prune rows a successor indexed (bootstrap.rs:23-41).",
        "invariants": [
          "The AND-to-OR fallback must be gated on the total estimate rather than the returned page, so every offset of one logical query uses the same MATCH string.",
          "The completion marker may only be written while the claim token is still held.",
          "A launch's first claim must ignore an existing marker because it owes a pruning pass, while later entrants adopt a peer's work.",
          "cwd must stay out of the FTS table - it is a JOIN filter, not indexed content.",
          "The title weight of 10.0 is what makes title matches outrank body matches; changing it silently reorders every result set."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "mixed - fail-open at the API edge (no manager or a blank query yields an empty response), fail-closed on real query errors (they propagate), and fail-soft for bootstrap (a failed or lost bootstrap only logs, rate-limited, and the completion marker is withheld so a later search retries).",
