        "wiringNote": "Wired only through a channel actor (`IndexManager`/`IndexManagerHandle`), spawned lazily on the first eligible code-navigation request, with a full-tree build running eagerly inside the actor while queries queue. THE SCOPE/EDGE GRAPH IS UNWIRED DEAD CODE: `build_scope_graph` and the only populator of the graphs map have ZERO call sites repository-wide, and the graphs map is never serialized. The shipped graph is a name-keyed occurrence map (symbol to list of relative-path and line) with bidirectional alias expansion. Host-side gating requires a web client, `x.ai/codeNavigation.enabled`, `features.codebase_indexing` (default enabled) and a git root. Note this is NOT the LSP path - the `x.ai/code/*` navigation methods route here, to tree-sitter, not to a language server."
      },
      {
        "name": "fuzzy-file-search-degradation-ladder",
        "what": "Fuzzy path search is built as an explicit three-state degradation ladder rather than as a feature that either works or does not. `FuzzyFileMatcher` owns an `ignore` git-aware walk feeding a `nucleo` matcher, and `FuzzyFileMatcherDaemon` drives it from a background thread over a bounded channel so callers poll for the current top-k (xai-fuzzy-file-search/src/lib.rs:28-29). The states are Full (pool plus keyed matching plus browsing), BrowseOnly (the pool was refused, so keyed queries return empty but an empty-query browse still works from a serial depth-1 walk), and Disabled (the daemon worker thread was refused, so every result is empty) (lib.rs:129-158, :277-315). Thread availability is probed by actually spawning and joining N threads before building the pools (lib.rs:196).",
        "invariants": [
          "`get()` on a Disabled daemon must report terminal-done with `generation = usize::MAX`, or a disabled search reads as perpetually pending once a query bumps the caller's minimum generation.",
          "The thread probe must join the previous walk first so it measures freed threads.",
          "A disabled matcher must not probe threads at all.",
          "`Drop` must join the walk before the matcher drops."
        ],
        "failurePolicy": "fail-soft, degrading rather than aborting - which is load-bearing because the process is built with `panic = \"abort\"`. An empty browse still returns results, a fully refused matcher returns empty, and a walk-thread spawn failure logs and yields no results for that walk. Errors are only ever tracing events; the public API has no error channel.",
